// Copilot review (PR #2516), comment 4113449699 + round-2 comment
// 4113556120: every existing thin-link f64-tuple-array gate either calls a
// lowerer PROBE entry point directly (--probe-filtered-body-reset-boundary
// etc. in main.sio) or runs a single file with no cross-module import at
// all -- so none of them exercises the real path module_loader.sio's
// thin_build_compiled_unit builds: an IMPORTED callee whose return type is
// a tuple with an f64 array slot, going through the actual multi-module
// frontend (--native-compile). `make_pair` is that callee: main.sio imports
// it with an ordinary `use`, then does arithmetic on its destructured
// `[f64; 2]` slot -- an integer-path misclassification here (from
// LOWER_FN_TUPLE_ARR_*'s name-only keying: see tta_other.sio's own
// same-named `make_pair`) corrupts that arithmetic via cvtsi2sd on the
// raw f64 bit pattern instead of an ordinary multiply.
pub fn make_pair() -> (i64, [f64; 2]) with Mut, Panic, Div, Alloc {
    (7, [10.5, 20.5])
}
